language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ de Bruijn sequence of order n on an alphabet of base symbols: a cyclic sequence of length base^n in which every string of length n occurs exactly once as a cyclic substring.
given base : int
given n : int
letting seq_len = base ** n
find de_bruijn : matrix indexed by [int(1..seq_len)] of int(0..base-1)

branching on [de_bruijn]
such that
$ every length-n string read cyclically from each start position is different, so each of the base^n strings occurs exactly once
allDiff([ (sum j : int(1..n) . de_bruijn[((i + j - 2) % seq_len) + 1] * base ** (n - j)) | i : int(1..seq_len) ])
